                        [39m  [38;2;255;255;255m2. [1mEach target code repository[22m, in its worktree at [38;2;177;185;249mC:\Users\haraujo\.building\data\projects\003-metro\worktrees\008/<repo-folder-name>[38;2;255;255;255m, checked out on branch                     [39m  [38;2;177;185;249m008-direction-filter[38;2;255;255;255m.                                                                                                                                                             [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;255;255;255mFor each of those with changes: stage everything first (including new/untracked files the Developer created — e.g. [38;2;177;185;249mgit -C                                                         [39m  [38;2;177;185;249m"C:\Users\haraujo\.building\data\projects\003-metro\worktrees\008/<name>" add -A[38;2;255;255;255m), review the staged diff, write a clear conventional commit message describing the change, and   [39m  [38;2;255;255;255mcommit it in that worktree. Skip any worktree with no changes. Everything is on the same branch name, [38;2;177;185;249m008-direction-filter[38;2;255;255;255m, in every repository, so the play reviews as one unit. [39m  [38;2;255;255;255mNever merge anything into the default branch yourself — the code branches are left unmerged for me, and Building merges the specs branch when the play closes.                    [39m                                                                                                                                                                                      [38;2;255;255;255mThen make sure I have a concrete way to test and validate what was implemented: check each changed worktree for existing testing/run instructions (README, CONTRIBUTING, docs)    [39m  [38;2;255;255;255mand follow them, or 