For each of those with changes: stage everything first (including new/untracked files the[1CDeveloper created — e.g.[38;2;177;185;249m[1Cgit -C[55X[9;3H"C:\Users\haraujo\.building\data\projects\003-metro\worktrees\008/<name>" add -A[38;2;255;255;255m), revi[1Cw the staged diff, write a clear conventional comm[2C message d[1Cscribing the change,[1Ca[1Cd  [10;3Hcommit it in that worktree. Skip [1Cny wo[1Cktree with no[1Cchanges. Eve[1Cything[1Cis on the same branch[1Cname, [38;2;177;185;249m008-direction-filter[38;2;255;255;255m,[1Cin every repository, so the play reviews as one unit.[11;3HNever merge anything into the default branch yourself — the code branches are left unmerged for me, and Building merges the specs branch when the play closes.[39m[12;3H[175X[38;2;255;255;255m
Then make sur[1C I[1Chave a co[1Ccrete way to t[1Cst and validate what was implemented: ch[1Cck[1Ceach changed worktr[1Ce for existing testing/run instruc[1Cions[1C(README,[1CCONTRIBUTING, docs)  [14;3Hand follow them, or write new ones if none exist. If the play has a web UI, include a direct link or the exact command to run it (point me at the worktree paths, since that is [15;3Hwhere the changes live).[39m[16;3H[176X[38;2;255;255;255m
