                                                            Before your first [38;2;177;185;249mnpm run test:e2e [mon this machine, run [38;2;177;185;249mnpx playwright install chromium [monce. The two new end-to-end tests are "cycles the direction filter" and "phone: the        minimised sheet follows the direction filter", both under "located near Portagem".                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      [1m2. Manual check in the browser[22m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          1. Run [38;2;177;185;249mnpm run dev [mand open [1mhttp://localhost:5173[22m (or whatever URL Vite prints).                                                                                                    2. Set a location near a stop served in both directions. In Chrome DevTools, open ⋮ → More tools → [1mSensors[22m → Location → Other…, then enter [1m40.2075, -8.4307[22m (Portagem). Reload and     allow location access.                                                                                                                                                           3. For a phone layout, turn on device mode (Ctrl+Shift+M) and pick a 390 px-wide device, such as iPhone 12/13/14.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       Check each of these:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    - [1mThe button appears.[22m Under "Heading to this stop" there is a button with a swap icon that reads [1mBoth directions[22m. The list shows buses in both directions, at most 4 rows, soonest    first.                                                                                                                                                                            - [1mIt cycles.[22m Each press moves to the next label:                                                                                                                                      - [1mBoth directions[22m                                                                                                                                                                   - [1mTo Vale das Flores, Serpins, Corvo[22m (or similar: the destinations of the outbound trips at this stop)                                                                              - [1mTo Coimbra B[22m                                                                                                                                                                      - [1mBoth directions[22m again                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 In each single-direction state, the list shows only that direction's buses.                                                                                                       - [1mLong labels are cut.[22m At 390 px the long "To Vale das Flores, …" label ends with an ellipsis and does not widen the sheet. Hovering the button shows the full label as a tooltip.  - [1mEmpty direction.[22m If a direction has no approaching bus at the moment, the list is replaced by "No buses in this direction right now." The header, the Scheduled badge and the       button stay, so you can cycle back.                                                                                                                                               - [1mThe map is not filtered.[22m While filtering, every bus marker stays on the map, the approaching buses keep their countdown tags, and the locate/reframe button frames the view as  
    before.[K
  - [1mMinimised phone sheet.[22m With the filter on "To Coimbra B", press [1mMinimise[22m. The single row is the soonest Coimbra B bus, with its Scheduled badge, and there is no direction      
    button. Press [1mExpand[22m: the button still reads "To Coimbra B".[K
  - [1mIt resets when the stop changes.[22m Set the filter to a single direction, then change the Sensors location to a different stop. The filter is back on "Both directions".[K
  - [1mNo button at one-direction stops.[22m At a stop served in only one direction (for example a line terminus), no direction button appears and the list behaves as before.               - [1mDesktop.[22m Turn off device mode. The side panel shows the same button and cycling works the same way. There is no minimise control on desktop.[K
